The reference semantics deliberately treats `sorted` as a trusted, concretely executable primitive, which fits this contract cleanly: a list is monotonic exactly when it equals its ascending sort or its descending sort. I’m using that implementation because it keeps both execution and the arbitrary-list proof aligned with the semantics’ intended proof boundary.
